IMPORTANT NOTE. This is a custom license. It is NOT approved by the Open Source
Initiative and does not meet the "Open Source" definition (it forbids certain
uses: see Article 5). It is "free" in the sense that all code stays public,
modifiable and free of charge. It is incompatible with most other licenses: do
not mix this project with code under conflicting terms. Have a lawyer review
this text before any high-stakes use.

1. Definitions.
 "Software": Imperial CodeCenter and every file distributed under this license
 (engine, API, crawler, interface, scripts, examples, documentation, images,
 configuration), in all versions. "Imperial": the Imperial organization and its
 contributors (https://imperial-corporation.pages.dev/icc). "You": any person
 or entity exercising rights under this license. "Derivative Work": any work
 that contains, adapts, translates, ports or modifies any part of the
 Software, including forks. "User Program": any software, service, script,
 module, plugin, application, website, library or system that incorporates,
 calls, imports, links to (statically or dynamically), embeds, runs, depends on
 or communicates with the Software through an interface specific to the
 Software (API, CLI, Python library, Rust module, internal protocol), excluding
 a generic web browser or HTTP client used by an end user to access an instance.
 "Combined Work": the Software or a Derivative Work together with all User
 Programs. "Source": the preferred form for making modifications, complete and
 readable, with build, test and installation scripts and documentation;
 obfuscated, minified-only, encrypted or compiled-only code is not Source.
 "Paid Project": any program, product, service, site, application, platform,
 project or activity (a) whose access, use, feature, version, content, hosting,
 support, maintenance or training is sold, rented, billed, subscribed or
 conditioned on payment, (b) funded in whole or part by advertising, data
 resale, subscriptions, commissions or any financial consideration tied to the
 use of the Software, (c) bundled in a paid commercial offer, even if apparently
 free ("freemium", free trial, a "community edition" accompanying a paid
 edition), or (d) distributed or operated by a for-profit legal entity as part
 of its commercial activity. "Donations": voluntary payments without
 consideration; not a payment under (a) if they condition no access, feature,
 benefit, priority or support. "Convey": distribute, publish, copy, transmit,
 host or make available to third parties by any means, including network
 access (online service, SaaS, public API).

2. Grant. Subject to all conditions, Imperial grants You a worldwide,
 royalty-free, non-exclusive, irrevocable (except under Article 12) license to
 use the Software for any purpose not forbidden by Article 5, study, copy and
 reproduce it, modify it and create Derivative Works, and Convey the Software
 and Derivative Works, modified or not. All other rights are reserved.

3. Mandatory attribution. You must keep in every copy, User Program and
 Derivative Work: the full license text, the NOTICE file, and the copyright,
 license and origin notices in files. You must clearly and visibly state that
 the work is "based on Imperial CodeCenter, created by Imperial" with the link
 https://imperial-corporation.pages.dev/icc in: the project README or home
 page, the documentation, the About page or footer of the user interface, the
 help screen or command-line version output, and the published package
 description, where they exist. The notice must remain legible and may not be
 hidden, made unreadable or removed. You must state the origin of the
 repository (the organization name, Imperial, and the address of the original
 project: the website above or the official repository published there). For a
 Derivative Work, you must also state that it was modified, by whom, and
 describe significant changes. The names "Imperial" and "Imperial CodeCenter",
 the logo and visuals are not licensed as trademarks; a Derivative Work must
 have a name clearly distinct from the original and must not suggest approval
 or endorsement by Imperial without written agreement. Credits of people
 listed in credit files must be kept.

4. Mandatory open code (no private or hidden code). Any Combined Work that You
 Convey — including through network access — must be made available to
 everyone, free of charge, with its complete Source, under this license
 ("reciprocity"). This applies in particular to every User Program: no code
 that uses the Software may remain private, closed, encrypted, obfuscated or
 secret once the Combined Work is Conveyed to a third party, including as a
 network-accessible service. Users of a network service must be able to obtain
 the corresponding Source (for example via a visible link in the interface).
 Source must be published no later than the first Conveyance, stay available
 as long as the work is Conveyed and for at least three (3) years afterwards,
 and be provided without registration, payment, NDA or restrictive clause. You
 may not impose any additional restriction: no more restrictive license, no
 technical measure preventing copying or modification (locking, DRM, mandatory
 runtime signatures), no contrary contract clause, no patent asserted against
 recipients. Purely private use: if You run or modify the Software for Yourself
 without Conveying it to anyone, You need not publish Your changes or User
 Programs; publication is required upon first Conveyance to a third party. Use
 within an organization (employees, members) counts as Conveyance: see Article 5.

5. Forbidden uses: no Paid Project; everything must be free. It is forbidden
 to use, integrate, modify, copy, Convey or run the Software, a Derivative Work
 or a Combined Work in, with, for or for the benefit of a Paid Project. The
 Software, Derivative Works, User Programs and any Combined Work must be made
 available free of charge, without any condition of payment, subscription,
 paid registration, mandatory advertising, data collection as consideration or
 "premium"/reserved version. Only Donations are tolerated. It is forbidden to
 sell or charge for the Software or a Combined Work; to charge for access,
 hosting, installation, configuration, support, maintenance, training or
 features related to the use of the Software; or to offer the Software as part
 of a paid good or service (including a bundle, subscription, paid
 marketplace, hardware sold with the Software preinstalled, or an integration
 service billed to a customer). Reimbursement of the actual, documented cost of
 a physical medium (for example a shipped storage device), without margin, is
 tolerated. Internal organizational use: a company, association or public body
 may use an instance internally provided that (i) the use is tied to no Paid
 Project, (ii) nothing is charged to anyone for this use, (iii) Article 4 is
 respected for everything Conveyed (internally or externally), and (iv)
 Articles 3 and 6 are respected. Expressly allowed, if the other articles are
 respected: personal, educational, scientific, non-profit associative and free
 community use; publication of free Derivative Works; contests or
 demonstrations with no cash prize for use of the Software. It is forbidden to
 circumvent this Article through structures (subsidiary, nominee, cross-license,
 dual license, or a third-party service providing the paid consideration in
 Your place) or by splitting the offer. Third-party AI models, providers and
 services that the Software calls (for example a pay-per-use AI API) do not
 make the Software paid: their own prices are not covered by this Article,
 provided You do not resell that access with the Software or draw any margin.

6. Transparency and contributions. Every modification You Convey must carry a
 clearly visible notice of the modification and its date. Unless otherwise
 agreed in writing, any contribution You voluntarily submit to Imperial for
 inclusion in the Software is licensed under this license ("inbound =
 outbound"); You warrant You have the right to submit it. Imperial may
 publish, modify or decline it.

7. Third-party components and content. The Software uses or may download
 third-party components (Python libraries, Rust crates, fonts, code fetched by
 the crawler from GitHub, examples) that remain under their own licenses; this
 license does not replace them and grants no rights over them. Code collected
 by the crawler remains the property of its authors under its original
 license. AI-generated answers, indexed data and content You add are not
 covered by this license; You are solely responsible for them.

8. Patents. Each contributor grants You a worldwide, royalty-free,
 non-exclusive, irrevocable (except Article 12) patent license over patent
 claims necessarily infringed by their contribution, to exercise the rights of
 Article 2. If You sue alleging that the Software infringes a patent, Your
 rights under this license end on the date of the suit.

9. No warranty. THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND,
 EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR
 PURPOSE, SECURITY, ACCURACY, AVAILABILITY OR NON-INFRINGEMENT, TO THE EXTENT
 PERMITTED BY LAW. AI-PRODUCED ANSWERS MAY BE WRONG: VERIFY THEM BEFORE USE.

10. Limitation of liability. TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, IMPERIAL AND ITS
 CONTRIBUTORS ARE NOT LIABLE FOR ANY DIRECT OR INDIRECT DAMAGES, LOSS OF DATA OR
 PROFITS, INTERRUPTION, SECURITY BREACHES OR OTHER DAMAGES ARISING FROM THE USE
 OR INABILITY TO USE THE SOFTWARE, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THEIR POSSIBILITY.
 NOTHING HEREIN EXCLUDES LIABILITY THAT CANNOT BE EXCLUDED BY LAW.

11. Your responsibility. You alone are responsible for complying with the laws
 applicable to Your use (personal data protection, copyright, export control,
 security rules, terms of AI providers and GitHub). You must protect secrets
 (API keys, tokens, passwords) and Your users' accounts.

12. Term and termination. The license lasts as long as You comply. On breach,
 it terminates automatically; it is reinstated (a) provisionally once You stop
 all breach, and (b) permanently if Imperial does not notify You within 60
 days after cessation. If Imperial notifies You of a breach for the first time,
 the license is permanently reinstated if You cure it within 30 days of
 notice. Termination does not affect those who received the Software from You
 as long as they comply; they receive their license directly from Imperial.
 A breach of Articles 3, 4 or 5 may also lead to enforcement (removal,
 publication of Source, cessation) and the remedies provided by law.

13. Distribution, sublicensing and versions. Each recipient receives a license
 directly from Imperial. You may not sublicense on different terms. Imperial
